    "summary": "I built a compact desk unit from four bases: three full bases at (0,0), (0,-1) and (1,-1), plus a north half base at (-1,0). A drawer sits in the cut face of the half base. The spike holding the platform stands at the corner where the three full bases meet. The planner found no spot for a spike in the first three-base layout, the one that includes the half base, so I added the fourth full base at (1,-1) to make one. The first spike I tried was the plain solid type, which can't carry a platform, so I used the mount type, which can, and fitted the small platform to it. All open faces are capped and the joints are bolted, for 22 parts in all. The build check shows no issues and no mesh clashes. I added no props because the brief didn't ask for any.",
    "outcome": "built"
